{# The paragraph of one misplaced-record repair, rendered from its evidence; see quality/demand.py::build_demand. #}
{% macro misplaced(e, min_ratio, low_mw, high_mw) %}
The timestamp {{ e.duplicated_utc|utc }} carries two values while {{ e.moved_to_utc|utc }} has none. The value {{ e.moved_mw|num(2) }} MW fits naturally between the neighbours of {{ e.moved_to_utc|utc }}, and {{ e.kept_mw|num(2) }} MW between those of {{ e.duplicated_utc|utc }}. The total path is {{ e.cost_mw|num }} MW in this assignment against {{ e.swapped_cost_mw|num }} MW the other way round: a ratio of {{ e.cost_ratio|num(1) }}. {% if e.runner_up is none %}{{ e.moved_to_utc|utc }} is the only hour without a record whose two neighbours are known: no other destination is possible.{% else %}Of the {{ e.destinations }} hours without a record whose two neighbours are known, the best after {{ e.moved_to_utc|utc }} is {{ e.runner_up.slot|utc }}, where the total path would be {{ e.runner_up.cost_mw|num }} MW: a ratio of {{ e.destination_ratio|num(1) }} to the chosen destination.{% endif %} The rule moves a value only if both values are inside the physical bounds ({{ low_mw|num }} to {{ high_mw|num }} MW), if the ratio between the two assignments is at least {{ min_ratio|num(1) }}, and if the destination is unambiguous: the best other hour without a record whose neighbours are known costs at least {{ min_ratio|num(1) }} times more, or there is none. Otherwise nothing moves, the hour stays an unresolved duplicate whose evidence names both possible destinations, and the gate fails. The value is therefore moved, and the hour is labelled "repaired" in the canonical series.
{%- endmacro %}
